scenario_text:
**CRM — Account: Bridgewater Dynamics**
ARR: $520K | Segment: Strategic | CSM: Aisha Patel | Contract signed: 18 months ago | SLA Tier: Premium

**Zendesk — Ticket #51033 (Open, P1)**
Subject: 'Production environment unavailable — 4hr+ outage' | Opened: June 22, 2026, 6:45 AM | Customer comment (June 22, 11:30 AM): 'Per our SLA, this exceeds the 99.95% monthly uptime commitment. Requesting 15% service credit as provided last October per case #38921. Our CFO has flagged this for the next board meeting.'

**Zendesk — Ticket #38921 (Closed, Oct 2025)**
Subject: 'Extended outage — credit request' | Resolution note (by prev CSM @jake.morrison, now departed): 'Approved 15% monthly credit as goodwill. Customer threatened escalation to CEO. VP Sales @rachel.torres approved via Slack DM. No formal exception filed.'

**Confluence — 'Service Credit Policy' (Page version 3, updated Jan 2026)**
Section 4.1: 'For Premium SLA customers, service credits are calculated at 10% of monthly fee per hour of downtime exceeding SLA, capped at 30% monthly fee. Credits require Director+ approval and must be filed through the Exception Request workflow in CRM.'
[Version history: v2 (Aug 2025) stated: 'Credits discretionary, approved by CSM manager or above. No cap specified.']

**Slack — #incidents (June 22, 2026, 7:02 AM)**
@jordan.kim: SEV-1 declared. Bridgewater and 3 other accounts affected. Root cause: DB failover didn't trigger.
@jordan.kim (8:45 AM): Failover completed. Services restoring.
@jordan.kim (9:15 AM): All clear. Total customer-impacting duration: 4 hours 12 minutes.

**Slack — DM between @aisha.patel and @rachel.torres (June 22, 2:10 PM)**
@aisha.patel: Bridgewater is asking for 15% credit like Jake gave them in Oct. New policy caps it differently but they're citing precedent.
@rachel.torres: Jake shouldn't have done that without a formal exception. I don't even remember approving it tbh. What does the current policy say?
@aisha.patel: 10% per hour over SLA, capped at 30%. So for 4hrs past the threshold it'd be... I need to calc.
@rachel.torres: Do what the policy says. If they push back, loop me in.
[No further messages]

**Google Doc — 'Bridgewater Dynamics Account Plan' (Last edited: 2 months ago)**
[RESOLVED COMMENT by @jake.morrison, Sep 2025]: 'Bridgewater's MSA has a custom SLA addendum — Section 8.4 overrides standard credit terms. They negotiated 15% flat per qualifying outage event, not per-hour. Legal reviewed. Check the contract attachment in SF.'
